 that people  highlight as to why bitcoin could be  valuable especially on a global stage  especially when there's geopolitical  risk uncertainty or chaos he ultimately  just decides that it's akin to money  laundering here listen exactly how he  describes it but if we're moving into a  world where trade breaks down what you  need for a global trade currency is  something that's large something that's  liquid and something where the  controlling body of the currency does  not regularly manipulate it so it can be  used with a degree of confidence that's  not bitcoin from the perspective of  someone in ukraine who is  fleeing the country and they can't get  money out of the atm because the atm's  literally on fire  and they get across the border and they  have access to their private wallet and  when they get across the border they can  then actually  expand economic resources that otherwise  they wouldn't have access to it's clear  that there's utility in that system why  wouldn't you just use a normal currency  for that scenario if you're going into a  system where there's a functional  society i don't see the utility i mean i  agree moving money out of a place  uh is something that bitcoin is used for  that's one of the reasons why a lot of  governments have banned it because it's  being used for smuggling the scenarios  where it is useful or not good enough  for it to be used regularly in any sort  of civilized system what you basically  just described is money laundering  now what's fascinating about this is  peter zeon he is one of the most well  respected geopolitical analysts in the  world and he continues to have very very  strong anti-bitcoin thought process now  whether he's right or wrong isn't for me  to decide or you ultimately my opinion  peter's opinion nor any of you watching  this your opinion as well it doesn't  matter the market will decide what  exactly is the true value of bitcoin  what i think is part of the missing part  of the conversation though is that  bitcoin continues to get adoption even  though so many different countries have  tried to ban it outlawed tax that are  regulated so many different individuals  around the world every single time they  get put into some sort of geopolitical  chaos or uncertainty they turn to  bitcoin helps them protect their wealth  helps them move it as seamlessly and  frictionless as possible and it also  gives them some sort of parachute a  lifeboat in these chaotic situations now  ultimately i don't know what's going to  end up happening but what i do know is  that every single fiat currency on the  planet  they have undisciplined rules they  change on a whim right now we're seeing  the european central bank literally say  hey we were very committed for eight or  nine years to negative interest rates  and a very specific monetary policy we  told the market these are what the rules  are going to be but now those rules are  changing and the ecb they're actually  not going to continue with the same  strategy they're now going to follow the  federal reserve they're going to make  capital more expensive and they're going  to raise that interest rate it's these  scenarios where bitcoin's programmatic  monetary policy the inability for any  individual or organization to actually  change bitcoin that highlights why  bitcoin may be valuable to so many  different people around the world now  again i don't know what's going to  happen but what i do know is on a  probability basis it's very likely that  bitcoin will continue to be adopted by  people around the world it doesn't  change no one can control it no one can  change the rules and that in today's  environment in all the global chaos  although geopolitical uncertainty and  all the undisciplined monetary and  fiscal policy probably is going to be  quite valuable
 

